changelog: |
  0.1.0 — initial kit, lifted from three fleet precedents rather than
  invented: zer0-mistakes' features/features.yml registry + test/visual/
  evidence-kit.mjs + .github/skills/visual-evidence (the evidence standard),
  it-journey's and barodybroject's features/features.yml (the same shape,
  minimal), and tools/issue-evidence.sh (screenshot-in-a-sandbox). What the
  kit adds is the fleet contract that ties them together: ONE features index
  schema (features/v1, a strict superset of every existing file, so the three
  precedents validate unchanged), declarative USER SCENARIOS an agent and a
  runner both read (verify/scenarios/*.yml — goto/click/fill/expect/
  screenshot, the steps a person would perform), a dependency-light Playwright
  runner that executes them into evidence bundles (test/evidence/<slug>/
  screenshots + report.json + README), a CI caller of the reusable
  fleet-verify.yml (scenarios on every PR; an OAuth Claude Code pass driving
  the live app through the Playwright MCP on `verify`-labelled PRs), and the
  repo-local verify-feature skill + verifier agent that make the loop
  runnable from a Claude Code session.
notes: |
  - Additive-only, like every kit: nothing the repo already has is overwritten.
    A repo with a legacy features/features.yml keeps it — the schema is a
    superset, so the hub index reads it as-is and coverage shows where the
    tests/scenarios/evidence links are missing.
  - SKILL.template.md and verifier.template.md are DEDICATED kit artifacts —
    the sanctioned exception to the agent-context 0.3.0 position that
    .claude/ layers never fan out: the kit IS the agent harness.
  - Snapshot to archive/ before editing runner.mjs or verify.yml so --upgrade
    can still recognise machine-seeded copies (same rule as the other kits).
  - Playwright needs a browser: `npx playwright install --with-deps chromium`
    (the reusable workflow does this; locally run it once).
